# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cna-house — ignored paths
#
# The openeggbert build rules fix a CLOSED list of build-directory names
# (AGENTS.md rule 2). They all live in the repository root; nowhere else is a
# build tree allowed, so the pattern is anchored and directory-only. An
# unanchored "build*" once swallowed a tools/ source file in CNA — do not
# un-anchor this.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/build/
/build-asan/
/build-ubsan/
/build-tsan/
/build-probe/
/build-consumer/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated content.
#
# content/ and content-fx/ are produced by cna-content from assets-src/ and are
# reproducible (cna-house.md §18.4). Nothing in them is ever committed.
#
# Corrected 2026-09-07 (HOUSE-00185). This block used to carve exceptions out of
# /content/ for a committed baseline -- Fonts/, Effects/, Textures/Debug/ -- and
# no such file ever existed there, because the baseline lives BESIDE ITS SOURCE
# in assets-src/Effects/*.xnb, which is what BL-04 says and what
# tools/effects/build_effects.sh produces. Keeping tracked files inside an
# otherwise-generated tree also makes an accidental `git add content/` far too
# easy. The build writes to ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/content anyway, so the top-level
# directory is only a placeholder.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/content/*
!/content/.gitkeep
/content-fx/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Authoring leftovers
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cna-content's own bookkeeping, if anyone runs it by hand with a source tree as the
# output root. tools/effects/build_effects.sh removes both; this is the safety net.
assets-src/**/.cna-content-manifest.json
assets-src/**/.cna-content.lock

assets-src/**/*.blend1
assets-src/**/*.blend2
assets-src/**/*.blend@

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs, saves and local run output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
/screenshots/
/test-output/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and tooling
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.vs/
*.swp
*~
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.cache/
compile_commands.json

# Generated world binaries (`HOUSE-00475`): `tools/ci/build_content.py --only world`
# writes them into the deployed content tree, and no compiled content is committed.
content/world/*.bin
